        <!-- Content Header -->
        <article style="margin-top: var(--space-32);">
            <span style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--size-small); color: var(--text-muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em;">Mechanistic Interpretability // Essay 03</span>
            <h1 class="hero-title" style="font-size: var(--size-display); margin-top: var(--space-8); margin-bottom: var(--space-24); line-height: 1.05;">Mapping the Residual Stream: How Models Track Internal Concepts</h1>
            
            <div style="display: flex; gap: var(--space-24); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-muted); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding-bottom: var(--space-24);">
                <span>Published: June 17, 2026</span>
                <span>Reading Time: 7 min</span>
                <span>Target: Activation Auditing</span>
            </div>

            <div class="article-body">
                <p>In standard feedforward network layers, activations overwrite each other at every step. Transformers, however, handle information routing completely differently. They use a continuous mathematical highway called the <strong>Residual Stream</strong>.</p>

                <p>Instead of transforming data monolithically, each attention head and Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) block writes its isolated output vectors straight onto this shared stream by simple addition. The residual stream functions as a massive, high-dimensional notice board that individual modules read from, append to, and refine across layers.</p>

                <h2>Linear Additions to the Hidden State</h2>
                <p>Because information aggregates via linear addition, we can express the absolute hidden state vector at any given layer $L$ as the flat summation of all prior layer contributions. Formally, this incremental vector accumulation is written as:</p>

                <div style="margin: var(--space-32) 0; text-align: center; font-size: var(--size-h3); font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--text-title);">
                    $$x_L = x_0 + \sum_{l=1}^{L} a_l + \sum_{l=1}^{L} m_l$$
                </div>

                <p>Here, $x_0$ represents the pristine token embedding, $a_l$ represents the localized attention vector update, and $m_l$ represents the dense channel adjustments from the MLP block. This architectural structure allows abstract semantic signals to travel intact through dozens of layers without disappearing or turning into noise.</p>

                <!-- Interactive Concept Reconstruction Workbench -->
                <section class="stream-sandbox" aria-label="Interactive Vector Addition Arena">
                    <span style="display:block; font-size: 11px; font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--text-muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em;">Vector Decomposition Arena // Layer State Synthesis</span>
                    <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--size-h3); color: var(--text-title); margin-top: var(--space-4); margin-bottom: var(--space-8); font-weight: 600;">Assemble the Concept Vector State</h3>
                    <p style="font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 0;">Toggle the architectural sub-layers below to see how adding their mathematical outputs constructs semantic concept trackers within the residual stream vector space.</p>

                    <div class="sandbox-interface">
                        <!-- Left Checkbox Controls Module -->
                        <div class="layer-controls" role="group" aria-label="Transformer Vector Layers">
                            <label class="control-row">
                                <input type="checkbox" id="layer-embed" checked disabled>
                                <div class="control-meta">
                                    <h4>Token Embedding</h4>
                                    <span>Vector base (x₀)</span>
                                </div>
                            </label>
                            <label class="control-row">
                                <input type="checkbox" id="layer-attn">
                                <div class="control-meta">
                                    <h4>Attention Layer 1</h4>
                                    <span>Context Mixer (a₁)</span>
                                </div>
                            </label>
                            <label class="control-row">
                                <input type="checkbox" id="layer-mlp">
                                <div class="control-meta">
                                    <h4>MLP Processing Block</h4>
                                    <span>Feature Extractor (m₁)</span>
                                </div>
                            </label>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Right Vector Space Value Tracking Canvas -->
                        <div class="vector-canvas-frame">
                            <div class="concept-bars">
                                <div class="concept-bar-wrapper">
                                    <div class="concept-label-row"><span>Concept: Code Syntax Structure</span><span id="txt-code">15%</span></div>
                                    <div class="concept-track-bg"><div id="bar-code" class="concept-fill" style="width: 15%;"></div></div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="concept-bar-wrapper">
                                    <div class="concept-label-row"><span>Concept: Urgent Priority Signal</span><span id="txt-urgency">5%</span></div>
                                    <div class="concept-track-bg"><div id="bar-urgency" class="concept-fill" style="width: 5%;"></div></div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            
                            <!-- Live State Vector Formula Readout -->
                            <div class="vector-formula-line" id="formula-readout">
                                Vector State: x = x₀
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <h2>Linear Probing and Concept Extraction</h2>
                <p>Because these underlying concept spaces organize linearly, mechanistic researchers can extract real-time tracking signals using a technique called <strong>Linear Probing</strong>. By training a simple linear classifier to look at a specific slice of the residual stream, we can read out the exact moment a model detects that code syntax is faulty, or notices that text has an angry or urgent tone.</p>

                <p>The model doesn't store these abstractions in separate, isolated nodes. Instead, it overlays them simultaneously across shared directional paths in a high-dimensional vector layout. This structural property—known as superposition—is precisely what gives modern transformer architectures their massive, adaptive processing power.</p>
